    "flat": [
      "Fourth-quarter net income fell 16% sequentially from the third quarter, and Markets & Investor Services revenue dropped 11% year over year in the same quarter, underscoring the trading business's sensitivity to short-term market conditions [c22][c6].",
      "Full-year noninterest expense grew 7% to $63.4 billion, and part of the headline year-over-year net income growth is a base effect from a one-time 2017 tax charge rather than purely operating improvement [c23][c17]."
    ],
    "short": [
      "The provision for credit losses rose 63% quarter over quarter, driven by reserve builds including card and Commercial & Industrial downgrades, which could be read as an early credit-normalization signal after several years of unusually low provisions [c8][c18].",
      "Asset & Wealth Management's assets under management fell 2% year over year on lower market levels, and Home Lending revenue fell 8% year over year on margin compression, showing pockets of the business already softening before the year closed [c9][c10]."
