  "editorial_notes": "Q4/FY2018 figures come from the firm's own 4Q18 earnings release and financial supplement (accession 0000019617-19-000002, filed 2019-01-15, before the 2019-01-16 cutoff); FY2014-FY2017 annual figures come from the collected XBRL facts (as originally filed in each year's Form 10-K). Two of the FY2017 history cells (total net revenue and noninterest revenue/expense) are shown using the *revised* comparative figures the firm published in the January 2019 release, because the firm adopted new revenue-recognition accounting standards effective January 1, 2018 and retrospectively restated 2017 comparatives [c16]; these differ modestly from the FY2017 amounts originally filed in the 2017 Form 10-K (captured separately via XBRL). Net income, EPS, provision for credit losses and net interest income were not materially affected by this restatement and are consistent across both vintages. Full-year 2017 net income also included a one-time $1.9 billion Tax Cuts and Jobs Act charge, which mechanically depresses the 2017 base used in year-over-year comparisons throughout this packet; this is flagged wherever growth percentages are quoted. All 'managed basis' non-GAAP figures from the source have been avoided in favor of reported-basis GAAP figures for the six required headline metrics, except where noted (segment revenue figures are presented on the firm's fully taxable-equivalent managed basis, its standard segment-reporting convention, and are labeled as such)."
